IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`

-- Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT) -- the procedure for stamp duty assessments and first home owner grant
-- decisions. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own actors and terms ("the taxpayer", "the person affected
-- by a relevant decision", "the decision maker", "the Commissioner"). The individual's questions are in sda-seat.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. This is not an official version of the Taxation Administration Act 2007. Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from reprint REPT039, as in force at 1 July 2024, deposited
-- at ../../../taxation-administration-act-2007/registers/source-bundle/
-- Taxation-Administration-Act-2007-NT-current-reprint-REPT039.txt, under the Northern Territory copyright policy of
-- 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 Oct 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). The reprint is more than two years old;
-- an amendment that commenced after 1 July 2024 is not in it.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 27 (amounts rounded down to 5 cents); s 21(4) (no reassessment more than 5 years after the
-- initial assessment, with its four exceptions); ss 107, 109-111 (who may object, to what, in writing within 60 days,
-- extension for a reasonable excuse); ss 113-117 (decision on the objection, then review by NTCAT or appeal to the
-- Supreme Court within 60 days; a first home owner grant decision goes to NTCAT only); s 128 (an objection does not
-- suspend recovery); ss 34-36 (interest on a tax default: the market interest rate is an INPUT, the premium is the
-- Act's 8%); ss 39, 41-43 (penalty tax: 25%, 10%, 75% or 95%, nil, the discretionary reductions, nil under $20, at
-- least 14 days to pay).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: investigations (Part 9), confidentiality (Part 10), returns and special arrangements (Part 6), recovery
-- (Part 7), refunds (Part 4) except as named, record keeping and offences (Part 8), NTCAT and Supreme Court procedure,
-- the MRA (royalty) branch of Part 11.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 2007 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 27 -- certain amounts to be rounded down`

-- s 27: "If the amount of a taxpayer's tax liability would, apart from this section, not be an exact multiple of 5c,
-- the amount must be rounded down by an amount not exceeding 5c to the highest exact multiple of 5c that is less than
-- that amount." "tax" includes a duty under a taxation law, interest and penalty tax (s 3(1)).
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the amount` TIMES 20) DIVIDED BY 20

§§ `s 21(4) -- the 5-year limit on reassessment`

-- s 21(4): "The Commissioner cannot reassess a tax liability more than 5 years after the initial assessment of the
-- liability, unless: (a) the reassessment is necessary to give effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal
-- under Part 11 ...; or (b) the taxpayer failed to make a full and true disclosure of all the facts and circumstances
-- affecting the liability and, as a result, the tax liability was assessed at a lower amount than it should have been;
-- or (c) the taxation law under which the liability arose authorises the making of a reassessment more than 5 years
-- after the initial assessment; or (d) the taxpayer applies, in writing, for the reassessment within 5 years after the
-- date of the initial assessment."
DECLARE `Reassessment facts` HAS
    `the date of the initial assessment`                                         IS A DATE
    `the date of the reassessment`                                               IS A DATE
    `it gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer failed to make a full and true disclosure and was assessed too low` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxation law authorises a reassessment after 5 years`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `r` IS A `Reassessment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner can make the reassessment` IF
        ((`r`'s `the date of the reassessment`) `is on or before` (`years after` 5 (`r`'s `the date of the initial assessment`)))
    OR  `r`'s `it gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal`
    OR  `r`'s `the taxpayer failed to make a full and true disclosure and was assessed too low`
    OR  `r`'s `the taxation law authorises a reassessment after 5 years`
    OR  `r`'s `the taxpayer applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years`

§§ `Part 11 Division 2 -- objections (ss 107, 109-111)`

-- s 107: a "relevant decision" is a taxation decision (an assessment, or a decision affecting a taxpayer's liability
-- to pay tax), a first home owner grant decision (a decision under the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 on an
-- application for the grant, requiring repayment of the grant, or relating to penalties or interest) or an agent
-- determination. A taxation decision does not include "(d) a decision not to make a reassessment" nor a negotiated
-- assessment ((f)-(h)). The "person affected" is the taxpayer, or for a grant decision the applicant for the grant.
DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `an assessment or reassessment of duty`
    `another decision affecting liability to pay duty`
    `a first home owner grant decision`
    `a decision not to make a reassessment`
    `a negotiated assessment`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant decision` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision not to make a reassessment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a negotiated assessment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 109(1): "A person affected by a relevant decision may object to the decision." (2): a reassessment "is only liable
-- to objection to the extent that it increases the assessed amount of the tax liability".
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `it is a reassessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount assessed before` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount assessed now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount open to objection` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`it is a relevant decision` `the decision`))
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `it is a reassessment`
         THEN `the greater of` 0 (`the amount assessed now` MINUS `the amount assessed before`)
         ELSE `the amount assessed now`

-- s 110(1): "The objection must be in writing and must be lodged with the decision maker within 60 days after notice
-- of the relevant decision is issued by the decision maker." (2): it "must state fully and in detail the grounds".
`the days to object` MEANS 60

-- s 111(1): "If the decision maker is satisfied an objector has a reasonable excuse for not lodging the objection
-- within the 60-day period, the decision maker may extend the time for lodgement." (2): only "on written application
-- for the extension setting out fully and in detail the reasons". The extension is the decision maker's to give; the
-- answer is conditional on it.
GIVEN `a written application for an extension, with full reasons, was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision maker is satisfied there is a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the time to object may be extended` IF
        `a written application for an extension, with full reasons, was made`
    AND `the decision maker is satisfied there is a reasonable excuse`

GIVEN `the decision maker extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days allowed to object` MEANS
    IF `the decision maker extended the time`
    THEN `the greater of` `the days to object` `the extended number of days`
    ELSE `the days to object`

§§ `Part 11 Division 3 -- review or appeal (ss 114-117)`

-- s 115(1): if the decision maker "decides to disallow the objection or allow it in part only, the objector may: (a)
-- apply to NTCAT for review ...; or (b) appeal to the Supreme Court". (2): "If the relevant decision that was subject to
-- the objection is a first home owner grant decision, the objector may only apply to NTCAT". (3), (4): not both.
DECLARE `Where the objection can go next` IS ONE OF
    `nowhere: the objection was allowed in full`
    `to NTCAT for review, or to the Supreme Court on appeal, but not both`
    `to NTCAT for review only`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `the outcome` IS AN `Objection outcome`
GIVETH A `Where the objection can go next`
`where the objection can go next` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `the objection is allowed in full` THEN `nowhere: the objection was allowed in full`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the decision`
        WHEN `a first home owner grant decision` THEN `to NTCAT for review only`
        OTHERWISE `to NTCAT for review, or to the Supreme Court on appeal, but not both`

-- s 116(1): an application to NTCAT "must be made by the objector within 60 days after the date on which the decision
-- maker gives notice of the decision". s 117(1): an appeal to the Supreme Court "must be commenced by the objector
-- within 60 days after" the same date. Both may be extended for a reasonable excuse (ss 116(2)-(4), 117(2)-(4)).
`the days to apply for review or to appeal` MEANS 60

-- The regulative rules. Clock: days. Objecting, applying and appealing are the person's choice, so not doing them is no
-- breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED); a late objection is simply not one the decision maker must consider (s 113(1): "If an
-- objection is properly made within the time allowed ..., the decision maker must consider the objection"). s 114(1):
-- the decision maker "must give written notice of the decision on the objection". No period is stated for deciding.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `the outcome` IS AN `Objection outcome`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
`the review or appeal after the decision on the objection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the objection can go next` `the decision` `the outcome`
    WHEN `nowhere: the objection was allowed in full` THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN `to NTCAT for review only` THEN
        PARTY `the person affected by the decision`
        DO    `apply to NTCAT for review of the decision on the objection`
        WITHIN `the days to apply for review or to appeal`
        LEST  FULFILLED
    WHEN `to NTCAT for review, or to the Supreme Court on appeal, but not both` THEN
            (PARTY `the person affected by the decision`
             DO    `apply to NTCAT for review of the decision on the objection`
             WITHIN `the days to apply for review or to appeal`
             LEST  FULFILLED)
        ROR
            (PARTY `the person affected by the decision`
             DO    `appeal to the Supreme Court against the decision on the objection`
             WITHIN `the days to apply for review or to appeal`
             LEST  FULFILLED)

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` IS
    IF (NOT (`it is a relevant decision` `the decision`))
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person affected by the decision`
         DO    `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail`
         WITHIN `the days allowed`
         HENCE (PARTY `the decision maker`
                MUST  `give written notice of the decision on the objection` `outcome`
                HENCE `the review or appeal after the decision on the objection` `the decision` `outcome`)
         LEST  FULFILLED

§§ `s 128 -- objection, review or appeal does not suspend recovery`

-- s 128: "An objection, application for review or appeal does not suspend: (a) the operation of a decision to which
-- the objection, application for review or appeal relates; or (b) the recovery of any tax or other amount that is,
-- assuming the validity and correctness of that decision, recoverable."
DECIDE `an objection suspends recovery of the tax` IS FALSE

-- The two run side by side: the duty stays payable by its due day while the objection runs.
GIVEN `the days to pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 128 -- the duty must still be paid while the objection runs` IS
        (PARTY `the taxpayer`
         MUST  `pay the duty`
         WITHIN `the days to pay`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "s 128: an objection does not suspend the recovery of the tax; unpaid duty is a tax default, with interest (s 34) and penalty tax (s 39)")
    RAND
        (`Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `the decision` `the days allowed`)

§§ `Part 5 Division 1 -- interest on a tax default (ss 34-36)`

-- s 34(1): "If a tax default occurs, the taxpayer is liable to pay interest on the unpaid primary and penalty tax."
-- (2): "at the statutory interest rate as in force from time to time"; (3): "calculated on a daily basis from the date
-- of the tax default to the date of payment". s 35(1): statutory rate = market interest rate + premium interest rate;
-- (2): the market rate is prescribed by regulation or the RBA's average 90-day bank bill yield for May of the preceding
-- financial year -- NOT DEPOSITED, so an INPUT; (3): the premium is "(a) up to (and including) 30 June 2008 -- 7%; and
-- (b) from (and including) 1 July 2008 -- 8%". s 36: "Interest is not to be charged if the amount of the accrued
-- interest is less than $20." READING: "a daily basis" is the annual rate divided by 365 for each day; the Act does not
-- say whether a leap year counts 366.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the premium interest rate on` MEANS
    IF `the day` `is on or before` (YMD 2008 6 30) THEN 7 ELSE 8

GIVEN `the unpaid primary tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the unpaid penalty tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the market interest rate, percent a year` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the tax default` IS A DATE
      `the date of payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on the tax default` MEANS
    IF `accrued` LESS THAN 20
    THEN 0
    ELSE `rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` `accrued`
    WHERE
        `days` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the date of payment` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the date of the tax default`
        `rate` MEANS `the market interest rate, percent a year` PLUS `the premium interest rate on` `the date of the tax default`
        `accrued` MEANS
            (`the unpaid primary tax` PLUS `the unpaid penalty tax`) TIMES `rate` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `days` DIVIDED BY 365

§§ `Part 5 Division 2 -- penalty tax (ss 39-43)`

-- s 39(1): "If a tax default occurs, the taxpayer is liable to pay penalty tax." s 41(1): "As a general rule, the
-- amount of penalty tax is 25% of the amount of the tax default." (2)(a): none if the Commissioner is satisfied the
-- default "arose from circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control (other than the taxpayer's financial incapacity ...)"
-- and the taxpayer "took all reasonable steps to rectify it"; (b): 10% if satisfied "the taxpayer took reasonable care
-- to comply"; (c): 75% if satisfied as to one, 95% if as to both, of "(i) ... intentional disregard ... of a taxation
-- law" and "(ii) ... deliberately concealed or suppressed information ... or hindered the assessment". Each is the
-- Commissioner's satisfaction: a FACT, answered conditionally. READING: the Act gives the exceptions no order; (a) is
-- taken first ("no penalty tax is to be imposed"), then (c), then (b), since a default from intentional disregard
-- cannot also be one where reasonable care was taken.
DECLARE `Penalty tax facts` HAS
    `the amount of the tax default`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the default arose from circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control and was rectified`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer took reasonable care to comply`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the default arose from intentional disregard of a taxation law`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `information was deliberately concealed or the assessment was hindered`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner investigated and the taxpayer cooperated fully`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `before any investigation, full and immediate disclosure avoided the need for one`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax rate, percent` MEANS
    IF `p`'s `the default arose from circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control and was rectified`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF     `p`'s `the default arose from intentional disregard of a taxation law`
            AND `p`'s `information was deliberately concealed or the assessment was hindered`
         THEN 95
         ELSE IF    `p`'s `the default arose from intentional disregard of a taxation law`
                 OR `p`'s `information was deliberately concealed or the assessment was hindered`
              THEN 75
              ELSE IF `p`'s `the taxpayer took reasonable care to comply`
                   THEN 10
                   ELSE 25

-- s 42: "Penalty tax is not to be imposed if the amount of the penalty tax would be less than $20."
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax after the $20 minimum` MEANS
    IF `the amount` LESS THAN 20 THEN 0 ELSE `rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` `the amount`

GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax` MEANS
    `the penalty tax after the $20 minimum`
        (`p`'s `the amount of the tax default` TIMES `the penalty tax rate, percent` `p` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 41(3): the Commissioner "may reduce the amount of penalty tax by up to 20% of the amount otherwise payable" if an
-- investigation is conducted and the taxpayer "cooperates fully"; "by up to 80%" if no investigation has commenced and
-- "the taxpayer's full and immediate disclosure ... avoids the need for an investigation"; "but if the taxpayer is
-- liable to penalty tax because of deliberate concealment or suppression of information, there is to be no
-- discretionary reduction". s 44 lets the Commissioner remit penalty tax "in whole or part" besides: that further
-- discretion is not bounded here.
GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Commissioner may reduce penalty tax by under s 41(3), percent` MEANS
    IF `p`'s `information was deliberately concealed or the assessment was hindered`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `p`'s `before any investigation, full and immediate disclosure avoided the need for one`
         THEN 80
         ELSE IF `p`'s `the Commissioner investigated and the taxpayer cooperated fully`
              THEN 20
              ELSE 0

GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` MEANS
    `the penalty tax after the $20 minimum`
        (`p`'s `the amount of the tax default` TIMES `the penalty tax rate, percent` `p` DIVIDED BY 100
         TIMES (100 MINUS `the most the Commissioner may reduce penalty tax by under s 41(3), percent` `p`) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 43: "Penalty tax must be paid by a taxpayer within the period (not less than 14 days) specified in a notice of the
-- assessment imposing the penalty tax." READING: a notice that names fewer than 14 days still leaves the taxpayer 14.
`the fewest days allowed to pay penalty tax` MEANS 14

GIVEN `the days specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days to pay penalty tax` MEANS
    `the greater of` `the fewest days allowed to pay penalty tax` `the days specified in the notice`

GIVEN `the days specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 43 -- pay the penalty tax within the period in the notice, at least 14 days` IS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `pay the penalty tax`
    WITHIN `the days to pay penalty tax` `the days specified in the notice`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "s 43: penalty tax must be paid within the period (not less than 14 days) specified in the notice of assessment; unpaid penalty tax bears interest (s 34(1))"
